 "answer": "**Part A**\nWe want to find $33^{853} \\pmod{211}$. Note that 211 is a prime number.\nBy Fermat's Little Theorem, $33^{210} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{211}$.\nSince $853 = 4 \\times 210 + 13$, we have:\n$33^{853} \\equiv 33^{13} \\pmod{211}$.\nCalculate powers of 33 modulo 211:\n- $33^2 = 1089 = 5 \\times 211 + 34 \\equiv 34 \\pmod{211}$\n- $33^3 \\equiv 34 \\times 33 = 1122 = 5 \\times 211 + 67 \\equiv 67 \\pmod{211}$\n- $33^4 \\equiv 34^2 = 1156 = 5 \\times 211 + 101 \\equiv 101 \\pmod{211}$\n- $33^8 \\equiv 101^2 = 10201 = 48 \\times 211 + 73 \\equiv 73 \\pmod{211}$\n- $33^{12} = 33^8 \\times 33^4 \\equiv 73 \\times 101 = 7373 = 34 \\times 211 + 199 \\equiv 199 \\equiv -12 \\pmod{211}$\n- $33^{13} \\equiv -12 \\times 33 = -396 = -2 \\times 211 + 26 \\equiv 26 \\pmod{211}$.\n\n**Part B**\nTrack month-by-month balance:\n- Month 1: $1200 - 250 = 950$. Fee: $950 - 8 = 942$. Interest: $942 \\times 1.005 = 946.71$.\n- Month 2: $946.71 + 300 = 1246.71$. Fee: $1238.71$. Interest: $1238.71 \\times 1.005 = 1244.90355$.\n- Month 3: $1244.90355 - 650 = 594.90355$. Fee: $586.90355$. Interest: $589.838068$.\n- Month 4: $589.838068 - 400 = 189.838068$. Fee: $181.838068$. Interest: $182.747258$.\n- Month 5: $182.747258 + 300 = 482.747258$. Fee: $474.747258$. Interest: $477.120994$.\n- Month 6: $477.120994 + 300 = 777.120994$. Fee: $769.120994$. Interest: $772.966599$.\n- Month 7: $772.966599 - 400 = 372.966599$. Fee: $364.966599$. Interest: $366.791432$.\n- Month 8: $366.791432 + 1100 = 1466.791432$. Fee: $1458.791432$. Interest: $1466.085389$.\n- Month 9: $1466.085389 + 700 = 2166.085389 \\ge 2000$. No fee. Interest: $2166.085389 \\times 1.005 = 2176.915816$.\n- Month 10: $2176.915816 + 700 = 2876.915816 \\ge 2000$. No fee. Interest: $2876.915816 \\times 1.005 = 2891.300395$.\n- Month 11: $2891.300395 + 300 = 3191.300395 \\ge 2000$. Interest: $3191.300395 \\times 1.005 = 3207.256897$.\n- Month 12: $3207.256897 + 700 = 3907.256897 \\ge 2000$. Interest: $3907.256897 \\times 1.005 = 3926.793181$.\n- Month 13: $3926.793181 + 450 = 4376.793181 \\ge 2000$. Interest: $4376.793181 \\times 1.005 = 4398.677147$.\n- Month 14: $4398.677147 - 250 = 4148.677147 \\ge 2000$. Interest: $4148.677147 \\times 1.005 = 4169.420533$.\n- Month 15: $4169.420533 + 700 = 4869.420533 \\ge 2000$. Interest: $4869.420533 \\times 1.005 = 4893.767636$.\nRounded to the nearest cent: 4893.77.\n\n**Part C**\nTotal marbles: $5 + 2 + 5 = 12$.\nNumber of ways to choose 3 marbles: $\\binom{12}{3} = \\frac{12 \\times 11 \\times 10}{6} = 220$.\nThe event \"at least two share a color\" is the complement of \"all three have different colors\".\nSince there are three colors (Red, Green, Blue), to draw all three of different colors, exactly one of each color must be drawn:\nNumber of ways: $\\binom{5}{1} \\times \\binom{2}{1} \\times \\binom{5}{1} = 5 \\times 2 \\times 5 = 50$.\nProbability of all different: $\\frac{50}{220} = \\frac{5}{22}$.\nProbability that at least two share a color: $1 - \\frac{5}{22} = \\frac{17}{22}$.\n\n**Part D**\nIncome = $68,250.\nTax before credit:\n- First $11,000 at 8%: $11,000 \\times 0.08 = $880.\n- $11,000 to $45,000 ($34,000) at 20%: $34,000 \\times 0.20 = $6,800.\n- Above $45,000 ($68,250 - $45,000 = $23,250) at 30%: $23,250 \\times 0.30 = $6,975.\nTotal base tax = $880 + $6,800 + $6,975 = $14,655.\n\nTax credit:\n- Base credit = $1,800.\n- Excess income over $60,000 = $68,250 - $60,000 = $8,250.\n- Credit reduction = $8,250 \\times 0.08 = $660.\n- Remaining credit = $1,800 - $660 = $1,140.\n\nTotal tax owed:\n$14,655 - $1,140 = $13,515.00.\n\nFINAL: 26; 4893.77; 17/22; 13515.00"
